--[[
	MP fork (§4 decision replication, increment B): client-side executor.

	When a scheduled server decision fires on this client's shared clock, the engine
	(CLevel::coop_dispatch_due_decisions) calls _G.mp_coop_on_decision, which is wired to
	on_decision() below by mp_client.on_client_level_start (the co-op thin client's Lua
	init hook — on_game_start never runs on a thin client, so this is registered there).

	subject_id : u16  - the object the decision concerns (an online NPC's id)
	kind       : u8   - decision kind enum (maps 1:1 to a gamedata executor)
	hex_args   : str  - kind-specific args, hex-encoded (binary-safe over Lua strings)

	For now this just logs receipt, proving the engine -> gamedata seam end to end. Real
	NPC control (resolve subject_id to a level object and drive its state_mgr movement
	target / combat enemy) plugs into on_decision.
--]]

-- Module-level (non-local) so mp_client can reference mp_coop_decision_client.on_decision,
-- which also triggers X-Ray to load this file on the client.
function on_decision(subject_id, kind, hex_args)
	printf("MP_COOP_DECISION_LUA: fired subject=%s kind=%s args=%s",
		tostring(subject_id), tostring(kind), tostring(hex_args))
	-- (real executor: local obj = level.object_by_id(subject_id); drive its state_mgr)
end
